-- ================================================================
-- FIXTURE — a generated generator, REFUSED BY CONTAINMENT.
--
-- THE MODEL IS NOT IN THE LOOP AT ALL. `rejected/generate_from_content.anthill`
-- is the attack that builds the generation PROMPT out of the mailbox; this is
-- the shorter one that skips generation entirely and returns the mailbox AS the
-- candidate program. Whatever `Prompt[Public]` guarantees about what a model was
-- asked is irrelevant to a `Source` no model ever wrote.
--
-- WHAT `Source`'s TYPE ASSERTS is that its text came from `generate`, which is
-- what its own header claims: "the only thing to do with one is submit it to a
-- `Checker`", and "for a program generated from a Public prompt" attacker data
-- did not influence it. Neither holds of a value anyone may mint from a `String`.
-- This is `forged_llm.anthill`'s finding at a second carrier — a capability-ish
-- type whose constructor was public, so the property its type asserts was
-- ADVISORY — and it is closed the same way, by `internal` (§8.6).
--
-- MEASURED BEFORE THE FIX: this exact file loaded clean (WI-20260829-MCKTE).
-- Note what does NOT refuse it. The taint labels do not: `Source` carries no
-- label by design. The rows do not: `{External, Error}` is honest, no model is
-- acquired and none is called. The refusal is a NAME RESOLUTION failure, so it
-- holds for a body carrying no effects at all.
--
-- AGAINST ANTHILL, NOT AGAINST THE HOST. §8.6 gates name resolution, so a host
-- binding reaching `guardians.Source.source` still mints one — as `generate`'s
-- own stand-in in `guardians_test.rs` must. "Anyone" above means any CANDIDATE.
--
-- PROVIDES NOTHING, like its sibling `generate_from_content.anthill`: the
-- generator side of the pipeline has no spec a candidate implements here, so
-- both are measured on the flat `assert_refused` path rather than through the
-- gate. The accepted control for the seal is `../checker.anthill`, which
-- RECEIVES a `Source` and loads (measured.md D3a).
-- ================================================================
sort guardians.agent.ForgingGenerator
  import anthill.prelude.{List, Error, External}
  import guardians.{Email, Mailbox, Source, join_texts}
  entity mk

  operation build(self: ForgingGenerator, box: Mailbox) -> Source
    effects {External, Error} =
      let msgs = Email.fetch(box)
      source(text: join_texts(msgs.map(lambda m -> m.body).collect()).raw)
end
